@@ -101,6 +101,25 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send notifications to people’s phones and desktops, so that everything landing in their tray reaches them even when Fizzy is closed.
+Push notifications are signed with a VAPID key pair, which is specific to your instance. Generate one with:
+
+```sh
+bin/rails push:keys
+```
+
+Then set the two values it prints in the `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` environment variables:
+
+```sh
+docker run --env VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=abcdef --env VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=123456 ...
+```
+
+Keep the pair around: browsers subscribe with the public key, so changing it means everyone has to turn notifications on again.
+Without these variables, push notifications are simply turned off, and people can keep using email notifications instead.
+People turn notifications on per device, from their notification settings.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
